From fdbb4cbb5c397c0931dcbcab7d0428605d815d5e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fabian Torres <46858378+fabiantorrestech@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 17:55:45 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Home: page indicator side, auto-hide fade, opacity, pill dots
 (inkOS-Patcher)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds six rows to Settings > Home, indented under "Enable Page Indicator"
and marked ✦ (patcher setting):
- Side: Auto (vanilla, opposite the apps), Left, Right. Left/Right draw
  the indicator in the side margin outside the apps, so it never covers
  an app label.
- Auto-hide: Off, 1s, 2s, 5s, 10s after the page last changed, the indicator
  fades out (600 ms). It fades back in (250 ms) on the next page change
  or when Home regains focus.
- Fades To: what auto-hide fades to: Nothing (0%) or 10-90%.
- Fade: Smooth or Instant (pops on/off in one frame, for e-ink).
- Opacity: 10-100% for the whole indicator while shown.
- Style: Classic (vanilla) or Pill (android_shortcut_hub's page dots,
  vertical: dimmed dots, current page as a long pill, light backing).

Defaults look exactly like vanilla. Only the side indicator changes; the
bottom Page Dots widget is untouched. Logic lives in
ui/PageIndicatorOptions.kt; upstream files get small hooks only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
